SURFACE-NAME COLLISION — finding + resolution (no silent drift, no 0130 damage)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TWO distinct web components are named `RecentActivity`:
    • features/dashboard/components/RecentActivity.tsx  → prompt P-0130 (a THREE-panel
      dashboard surface: activity feed + battery-trend Swift Chart + fleet performance).
      ALREADY SHIPPED + locked: feature-views/RecentActivity.{swift,Types,Adapter,Model,
      Views,States,Charts,Previews,Tests,ModelTests}.swift + RecentActivity.strings, with
      p4-apple-feature-views-0130-RecentActivity.log ending EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE.
    • features/vehicles/components/RecentActivity.tsx   → THIS prompt P-0277 (a TWO-panel
      Recent Drives + Recent Charges feed). A genuinely different component.
  Both prompts nominate the same native output `feature-views/RecentActivity.*` and the
  same module (TeslaSync). Overwriting 0130 would destroy a locked, passing surface
  (Covenant #2 scope-narrowing, #9 silent drift) and break its co-located tests; two
  Swift types named `RecentActivity` cannot coexist in one module.
  RESOLUTION (the only non-destructive option): ship the vehicles surface with distinct
  `VehicleRecentActivity*` Swift symbols + a distinct i18n table "RecentActivityVehicles",
  in files `RecentActivity.Vehicles.*` — which DO match the allowed `RecentActivity.*`
  glob (the glob's `*` matches `Vehicles.<x>.swift`) and the feature-views source glob in
  project.yml, so both surfaces compile side-by-side. Grep confirmed zero pre-existing
  `VehicleRecentActivity*` / `RecentDrivesPanel` / `InMemoryVehicleRecent*` symbols.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAPPING (web → native)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  props:  RecentActivity({ drives, sessions }) (web parent derives via useDriving /
            useCharging) + useUnits().unitPrefs.distance
            → one VehicleRecentActivityUpdate snapshot pushed by a
              VehicleRecentActivitySource (P1/S8); the projection derives the two panels.
            → convertDistanceFromSI divisor carried as a value-typed `distanceDivisor`
              (1609.344 for mi, 1000 for km) so the projection stays pure + KMP-free,
              exactly the dashboard surface's value-typed-factor approach.
  shell:  2× <GlassPanel className="p-6"> in a grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2
            → VehicleRecentActivityGlassPanel (Color.TS.surfaceGlass + TSRadius.lg +
              Color.TS.border stroke). Side-by-side on a regular width, stacked on a
              compact width (horizontalSizeClass) — the same responsive intent.
            → each panel wrapped in TSFadeIn(delay: 0.25 / 0.27) — the web per-panel
              FadeIn delays, reduce-motion-safe.
  panel1: Recent Drives — Route glyph (cyan) + t('common.recentDrives') + Link("/drives")
            t('common.viewAll') + ChevronRight; drives.slice(0,5) rows OR
            t('common.noDrives') "No drives recorded yet"
            → VehicleRecentActivityPanel(icon road.lanes, tint accent): header + rows
              or the per-panel empty. Drive row: IconBox(cyan, road.lanes) +
              "{convertDistanceFromSI(distance_m,unit)} {unit}" (AnimatedNumber, 1 dp) +
              <TimeStamp start_ts> + InlineMetric clock "{floor(s/3600)}h
              {fmtInt(floor((s%3600)/60))}m" + (both SoC present) "{start}% → {end}%".
              Whole row is a Button → onNavigate(.drive(id)) (web row <Link>).
  panel2: Recent Charges — BatteryCharging glyph (emerald) + t('common.recentCharges') +
            Link("/charging") t('common.viewAll'); sessions.slice(0,5) rows OR
            t('common.noCharges') "No charging sessions recorded yet"
            → VehicleRecentActivityPanel(icon battery.100.bolt, tint statusSuccess).
              Charge row: IconBox(green, bolt.fill) + "{convertEnergyFromSI(wh,'kWh')} kWh"
              (1 dp) + <TimeStamp start_ts> + clock "{Xh Ym}" + (end SoC present)
              "{start}% → {end}%". Button → onNavigate(.charge(id)).
  fmt:    fmtNumber/safeNumber → number/safe (NumberFormatter .decimal, .halfUp, grouping,
            non-finite→0); fmtInt → int; convertDistanceFromSI → distanceFromSI(÷divisor,
            zero-safe); convertEnergyFromSI('kWh') → energyKwhFromWh (÷1000); <TimeStamp>
            relative + absolute bodies (relative "Xm/Xh/Xd ago"/"Just now"/short date;
            absolute month-abbrev day hour minute) with the unselected style offered to
            VoiceOver (the web tooltip alternate). Charge duration stored SI seconds
            (web reads duration_min; Xh Ym renders identically) — column stays SI-canonical.
  i18n:   5 web t() keys (common.recentDrives|recentCharges|viewAll|noDrives|noCharges) →
            VehicleRecentActivityStrings facade, table "RecentActivityVehicles". Symbols
            (%, →, h, m, kWh, the unit label) are locale-neutral literals exactly as the
            web builds them in template strings.

STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface):
  loading  → VehicleRecentActivityLoading (two redacted TSSkeleton panels, responsive,
             reduce-motion safe)
  content  → the two panels, each with its OWN internal empty (web per-panel
             "No drives…" / "No charging sessions…") — never blank
  empty    → VehicleRecentActivityEmpty (ContentUnavailableView, friendly message) when
             the whole snapshot resolves with no drives AND no charges
  error    → VehicleRecentActivityError (QueryError-equiv, Retry → model.refresh())
  stale    → freshness chip (Stale) + connectivity banner + ONE guarded auto-refresh
             (re-armed on return to live)
  offline  → freshness chip (Offline) + banner; keeps cached panels, no refetch
  (The web component itself only splits each panel content/empty; the loading/error/
   stale/offline envelope the parent owns is reproduced here so no state is a blank box.
   Chip + banner show ONLY when not live, keeping the healthy state as clean as the web.)
a11y: container summary (surface label + recent-drive/recent-charge counts, or friendly
  empty); per-row VoiceOver "{value}, {time}, {duration}[, {socRange}]" with .isButton;
  icons accessibilityHidden; reduce-motion fade gate (TSFadeIn); Dynamic Type via system
  fonts/tokens; monospacedDigit + fixedSize on values.
telemetry: P1/S11 view.opened(surface:"RecentActivity") emitted once on appear (slug per
  prompt §8; executed-once proven at §6).
binding: P1/S8 VehicleRecentActivitySource seam (production impl over the shared driving/
  charging state holders + useUnits prefs); the view performs NO networking. Previews/tests
  drive InMemoryVehicleRecentActivitySource.

